  data:  # e28d
    kind: work_item  # e28d
    title: "serve: client-side encrypted Yjs updates (fragment key -> HKDF -> AES-256-GCM), server as opaque relay; precondition for any off-localhost exposure"  # e28d
    status: todo_soft  # e28d
    priority: 4  # e28d
    parent:  # e28d
    tags:  # e28d
    - tracker_serve  # e28d
    - security  # e28d
    - yjs  # e28d
    - plazaflow  # e28d
    - someday  # e28d
    isbefore: []  # e28d
    duplicate_of: []  # e28d
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e28d
    pr_ref:  # e28d
    description: "## What\nClient-side encryption of Yjs updates for the live tracker document, with the server as an opaque relay that stores and forwards ciphertext it cannot read: key material from a URL fragment -> HKDF-SHA-256 -> AES-256-GCM, the fragment scrubbed from the URL after key derivation (history.replaceState). This is PlazaFlow's v0.2 step (custom relay replacing y-websocket because y-websocket merges plaintext updates) rehearsed on the tracker, and it is the precondition for exposing the sync endpoint (item D) anywhere but 127.0.0.1.\n## Preconditions (isbefore edges)\nWI-hopip (serve write-API auth) and WI-sunan (tracker self-claims covering serve) must be done first: an encrypted relay does not substitute for authenticating the write path, and the self-claims must state what the relay can and cannot see.\n## Done when\nRelay-side storage holds only ciphertext (test: snapshot bytes contain no plaintext field values); two clients with the fragment converge; a client without it cannot decrypt; the AAD binds tracker-root id and key epoch. Document the honest security model (what this does NOT protect) in serve.py and SECURITY.md.\n## Context\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_10162026_2318.md section 4; PlazaFlow spec v0.2 (pf-prelim) §Encryption; ADR-0019 §Security."  # e28d
    fields: {}  # e28d
- op: discuss  # 3e2b
  at: '2026-11-01T22:22:32Z'  # 3e2b
  by: agent  # 3e2b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 3e2b
  clock: 2  # 3e2b
  nonce: 3e2b  # 3e2b
  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/tool1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. Reviewed 2026-11-01 against ADR-0062 (2026-10-29). Still valid: ADR-0062 section 6 defers encryption to WI-pufun and hard-codes 127.0.0.1 until WI-sunan, so this remains the precondition for off-loopback exposure. WI-hopip is done; WI-sunan and WI-vojil are todo_hard isbefore predecessors. In conflict: sections 2 and 5 require serve itself (WI-lakid projection, WI-rudat bridge emitting ops) to read every update, and they reject a relay. A server that 'stores and forwards ciphertext it cannot read' therefore cannot also run the bridge. The design must pick: a client-side bridge, or a key-holding server (not opaque). SECURITY.md exists at the repo root. MECHANISM: ADR-0062 puts the projection, the write-back bridge and the token table inside serve's process, which must read plaintext Y.Doc updates; an opaque relay that cannot decrypt contradicts that design. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-divug."  # 3e2b
